name: paradigm
description: "The Paradigm Claude Code plugin: hooks (enforcement), skills, agent definitions and the plugin's MCP server launch. Hook scripts are generated from packages/paradigm/src/commands/hooks/scripts by scripts/generate-hooks.mjs; edit the canonical copies, not these."
context:
  - ".claude-plugin/plugin.json version must equal @a-company/paradigm's (tests/plugin-version.test.ts): Claude Code caches installs by version"
  - "scripts/ is generated except paradigm-mcp-launch.cjs and migrate-to-plugin.sh (paradigm-resolve.sh, the hooks' CLI lookup, is generated like the other hook scripts)"
# Key files touched:
# - .mcp.json
# - scripts/paradigm-mcp-launch.cjs
components:
  paradigm:
    description: "The Claude Code plugin bundle (hooks/hooks.json, skills/, agents/, scripts/) installed from the a-paradigm marketplace"
    tags: [plugin, claude-code]
  paradigm-mcp-launch:
    description: |
      Starts the plugin's MCP server (.mcp.json runs `node scripts/paradigm-mcp-launch.cjs <project>`).
      The project is argv[2] if it is an existing directory, else an expanded CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR, else
      cwd (the fallback is said on stderr). Finds an @a-company/paradigm package in the hooks' order
      (scripts/paradigm-resolve.sh): the project root's node_modules first (never a parent folder; the
      package.json must name @a-company/paradigm), so a project that pins Paradigm gets its version; then
      paradigm-mcp on PATH; then `npx --yes --prefer-offline` pinned to plugin.json's version, run from
      <os.tmpdir()>/paradigm-mcp-npx-<uid> (created on demand with a {"private":true} package.json that
      stops npm's walk up; a folder owned by someone else is replaced by a fresh mkdtemp one), 120 s
      timeout, failures (error / signal / exit status) on stderr. npx only locates the package: it runs
      `node <launcher> --locate` (node is the command word, the launcher an argument npm escapes), which
      prints the entry. The launcher runs the entry with node in the project, with its own env; a version
      that differs from the plugin's goes to stderr. Why: npm 11 applies the nearest package.json's
      devEngines to npx, so npx run from a pnpm-only project (onFail "error") exits EBADDEVENGINES;
      `--prefix` was rejected because it also moves npm's global prefix and globalconfig.
    tags: [plugin, mcp, launch]
